{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wt5yhdxiUGn8W4NuoWQ3bR","type":"tool_result","content":"160\tdef is_disabled() -> bool:\n161\t    \"\"\"Return True if ``CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE=1``.\"\"\"\n162\t    return os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE\", \"\") == \"1\"\n163\t\n164\t\n165\tdef _audit_dir_from_env() -> Path:\n166\t    \"\"\"Resolve the audit dir, aligned with audit_emit._audit_dir().\n167\t\n168\t    Precedence mirrors audit_emit + spool_writer so the HMAC sidecars\n169\t    (key, last-hmac, chain-length) co-locate with the audit log + its\n170\t    FileLock under the coherent-env contract (processes writing one log\n171\t    share the same CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR, or all run pure-$HOME):\n172\t\n173\t      ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH`` parent (the EFFECTIVE log — most specific,\n174\t      rail r2 D) -> ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` -> ``CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR`` ->\n175\t      the single family resolver (``_lib/runtime_paths``, PLAN-182 W1:\n176\t      ``$HOME/.claude/projects/<native-slug>/``).\n177\t\n178\t    Honoring CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR closes a latent split (S168): a LOG_DIR-only\n179\t    process resolved its FileLock under LOG_DIR but its chain-length counter\n180\t    under $HOME, so two such processes (same $HOME, different LOG_DIR)\n181\t    shared one counter while holding different locks — a lost counter\n182\t    increment that weakens tail-truncation detection.\n183\t    \"\"\"\n184\t    # PLAN-182 W1 rail r2 D: a familia segue o LOG EFETIVO — PATH (mais\n185\t    # especifico) vence DIR, igual a audit_emit._log_path/_log_family_dir,\n186\t    # spool_writer e audit_log. Com AMBOS setados, log+lock+key+sidecars\n187\t    # ficam TODOS no parent do PATH; a ordem antiga (DIR primeiro) partia\n188\t    # a familia em dois diretorios.\n189\t    p = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH\")\n190\t    log_dir = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR\")\n191\t    if p:\n192\t        path_parent = Path(p).resolve().parent\n193\t        # rail r9 P1 — PRESERVACAO DE CADEIA EXISTENTE: numa instalacao\n194\t        # que JA rodava com DIR e PATH divergentes, a chave/sidecars\n195\t        # vivem sob DIR (a precedencia antiga). Trocar a precedencia sem\n196\t        # olhar cunharia uma chave NOVA ao lado do log e NENHUMA das duas\n197\t        # verificaria a cadeia inteira. Regra: se a chave legada existe\n198\t        # sob DIR e ainda NAO existe no destino, a familia CONTINUA no\n199\t        # DIR (breadcrumb nomeando a config); a migracao dos sidecars e\n200\t        # decisao de cerimonia, nunca um efeito colateral de import.\n201\t        if log_dir:\n202\t            legacy_dir = Path(log_dir)\n203\t            preserve = False\n204\t            try:\n205\t                if legacy_dir.resolve() != path_parent:\n206\t                    # rail r10 P1a: QUALQUER sidecar legado conta, nao so a\n207\t                    # audit-key com nome default — uma instalacao com\n208\t                    # CEO_AUDIT_KEY_PATH explicito ainda tem last-hmac e\n209\t                    # chain-length sob LOG_DIR, e ignora-los reiniciaria a"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f7338f3-f544-4c31-91bf-9348522f093d","uuid":"b97310d2-4c5e-475a-8bfc-cfde7c40bd00","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:06:10.393Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_hmac.py","content":"def is_disabled() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if ``CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE=1``.\"\"\"\n    return os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE\", \"\") == \"1\"\n\n\ndef _audit_dir_from_env() -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Resolve the audit dir, aligned with audit_emit._audit_dir().\n\n    Precedence mirrors audit_emit + spool_writer so the HMAC sidecars\n    (key, last-hmac, chain-length) co-locate with the audit log + its\n    FileLock under the coherent-env contract (processes writing one log\n    share the same CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR, or all run pure-$HOME):\n\n      ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH`` parent (the EFFECTIVE log — most specific,\n      rail r2 D) -> ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` -> ``CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR`` ->\n      the single family resolver (``_lib/runtime_paths``, PLAN-182 W1:\n      ``$HOME/.claude/projects/<native-slug>/``).\n\n    Honoring CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR closes a latent split (S168): a LOG_DIR-only\n    process resolved its FileLock under LOG_DIR but its chain-length counter\n    under $HOME, so two such processes (same $HOME, different LOG_DIR)\n    shared one counter while holding different locks — a lost counter\n    increment that weakens tail-truncation detection.\n    \"\"\"\n    # PLAN-182 W1 rail r2 D: a familia segue o LOG EFETIVO — PATH (mais\n    # especifico) vence DIR, igual a audit_emit._log_path/_log_family_dir,\n    # spool_writer e audit_log. Com AMBOS setados, log+lock+key+sidecars\n    # ficam TODOS no parent do PATH; a ordem antiga (DIR primeiro) partia\n    # a familia em dois diretorios.\n    p = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH\")\n    log_dir = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR\")\n    if p:\n        path_parent = Path(p).resolve().parent\n        # rail r9 P1 — PRESERVACAO DE CADEIA EXISTENTE: numa instalacao\n        # que JA rodava com DIR e PATH divergentes, a chave/sidecars\n        # vivem sob DIR (a precedencia antiga). Trocar a precedencia sem\n        # olhar cunharia uma chave NOVA ao lado do log e NENHUMA das duas\n        # verificaria a cadeia inteira. Regra: se a chave legada existe\n        # sob DIR e ainda NAO existe no destino, a familia CONTINUA no\n        # DIR (breadcrumb nomeando a config); a migracao dos sidecars e\n        # decisao de cerimonia, nunca um efeito colateral de import.\n        if log_dir:\n            legacy_dir = Path(log_dir)\n            preserve = False\n            try:\n                if legacy_dir.resolve() != path_parent:\n                    # rail r10 P1a: QUALQUER sidecar legado conta, nao so a\n                    # audit-key com nome default — uma instalacao com\n                    # CEO_AUDIT_KEY_PATH explicito ainda tem last-hmac e\n                    # chain-length sob LOG_DIR, e ignora-los reiniciaria a","numLines":50,"startLine":160,"totalLines":1230}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wt5yhdxiUGn8W4NuoWQ3bR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
