y:189) and spool_writer. The profiler leaves these variables in place: CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH, CEO_AUDIT_LOG_LOCK, CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ERR, CEO_AUDIT_KEY_PATH, CEO_AUDIT_LAST_HMAC_PATH, CEO_AUDIT_CHAIN_LENGTH_PATH and CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR.\n- Failure scenario: a maintainer or adopter with CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH exported runs \"profile-opus-4-7.py --hook-latency\" (N=200 by default). The five corpus entries make roughly 1,400 hook runs, counting the seed runs. Every check_agent_spawn, check_anti_ceo_overhead and check_output_secrets event from those runs is appended to the LIVE audit log and HMAC chain under session \"profile_latency\".\n- Relation to the base re-pass: this is the same defect the v1.4.3-rc.1 re-pass ranked P1 in diagnose-output-hook.py. Condition 3(a) fixed it only there, by removing _CHILD_LOCATION_CARRIERS (diagnose-output-hook.py:27-34). That script even imports this profiler module, but the profiler's own gate was not fixed.\n- Minimal fix: in latency.py, remove the same list of variables from base_env as diagnose-output-hook.py:27-34 (or as the list in test_isolation.py), before HOME and CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR are set per entry. Also set CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR per entry, and add a test that runs the profiler with CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH set and checks that the real log stays the same.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. Honesty: two docstrings describe the old snapshot write path.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_precompact_parts/snapshot_core.py:335-340, and the docstring of check_precompact_continuity.py:57-63.\n- Both say the snapshot is handed to store.set as a str so that the store's redactor runs. The code at snapshot_core.py:424-426 now redacts each field first and passes BYTES. It passes a str only when _lib.redact fails to import.\n- Secrets are still redacted. One side effect: on the bytes path, state_store's \"redacted\" column records 0 even when a field was redacted.\n- Fix: update both docstrings to describe the field-level redaction and the bytes write.\n2. The PreCompact facade loses its module docstring.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_precompact_parts/__init__.py:16.\n- exec() of each part file stores that part's own docstring as the facade's __doc__, so check_precompact_continuity.__doc__ ends up as runtime.py's one-line docstring instead of the 85-line contract. audit_log.py:315/328 saves and restores __doc__ for exactly this reason; this facade does not.\n- I found no production code that reads it. Fix: save __doc__ before install and restore it after.\n3. Project-root resolution can pick a nested directory.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_precompact_parts/snapshot_core.py:53.\n- _resolve_project_root takes the nearest ancestor that has a .claude/ directory before it looks at CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR. When the session's working directory is inside a nested .claude/ tree (a monorepo package, a fixture), the plan lookup and the ceremony glob move there. So does the hysteresis-marker write, when CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS is set and the sidecar identity check passes.\n- The hook fails soft and the marker write is opt-in. Fix: prefer CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR when the working directory is inside it, and apply the same rule in the PostCompact reader.\n4. Stale help text: .claude/hooks/_lib/_reality_ledger_parts/dispatch.py:136 says \"Default: all 5\" for --detector, but DETECTOR_REGISTRY has 6 detectors (estimate_drift is the sixth). Cosmetic; probably carried over unchanged.\n5. A second, unused action registry (cross-reference to another payload).\n- _audit_emit_parts/actions.py defines a second _KNOWN_ACTIONS (actions_core | actions_extended). Nothing imports it, and it is not in the install list of audit_emit.py:415-452.\n- The writer checks against the literal set in the facade (writer.py:558 against audit_emit.py:45). The fallback that _read_known_actions adds in this payload (audit_actions.py) can only resolve a _KNOWN_ACTIONS that a module in the install list exports, so it is inert today.\n- Risk: two sources of truth. An action added only to actions_core.py or actions_extended.py would be dropped silently. Fix: delete actions.py and its two data modules, or make the facade take _KNOWN_ACTIONS from it."},"ttft_ms":11106,"type":"result","duration_ms":447066,"uuid":"5017a094-156d-44c1-af9f-e0f58badf566","ttft_stream_ms":8293,"time_to_request_ms":219,"first_content_frame_ms":8293,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":70,"outputTokens":38589,"cacheReadInputTokens":5115752,"cacheCreationInputTokens":181704,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.248842399999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":24641,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":181704,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-20T15:54:23.997Z"}
